{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q001", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 1, "question_type": "fill_blank", "score": 3, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["极限"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q001.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-1.png"], "answer": "$-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}$", "explanation": "Rationalize the numerator and cancel $(x-1)$:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3-x}-\\sqrt{1+x}=\\frac{-2(x-1)}{\\sqrt{3-x}+\\sqrt{1+x}}.\n$$\n\nThen substitute $x=1$.", "methods": ["有理化"]}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q002", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 2, "question_type": "fill_blank", "score": 3, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["法线方程"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q002.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-1.png"], "answer": "$x-2y+2=0$", "explanation": "Differentiate implicitly:\n\n$$\ne^{2x+y}(2+y')+\\sin(xy)(xy'+y)=0.\n$$\n\nAt $(0,1)$ we get $y'=-2$, so the normal slope is $1/2$.", "methods": ["隐函数求导"]}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q003", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 3, "question_type": "fill_blank", "score": 3, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["定积分", "奇偶性"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q003.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-1.png"], "answer": "$\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}$", "explanation": "The term $x^3\\cos^2x$ is odd, so its integral on the symmetric interval is $0$.\nReduce the rest to $2\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\sin^2x\\cos^2x\\,dx$.", "methods": []}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q004", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 4, "question_type": "fill_blank", "score": 3, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["微分方程"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q004.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-1.png"], "answer": "$y=x\\arcsin x-\\dfrac12$", "explanation": "Recognize the left-hand side as $\\dfrac{d}{dx}(y\\arcsin x)$, integrate once, and use the given point.", "methods": ["乘积求导"]}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q005", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 5, "question_type": "fill_blank", "score": 3, "module": "线性代数", "topics": ["线性方程组", "秩"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q005.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-1.png"], "answer": "$-2$", "explanation": "The system has infinitely many solutions iff the coefficient matrix and augmented matrix have the same rank, smaller than $3$.\nRow reduction gives $a=-2$.", "methods": []}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q006", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 6, "question_type": "choice", "score": 3, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["分段函数", "复合函数"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q006.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-1.png"], "answer": "B", "explanation": "The values of $f$ are only $0$ and $1$, and both satisfy $f(0)=f(1)=1$.", "methods": []}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q007", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 7, "question_type": "choice", "score": 3, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["无穷小比较", "等价无穷小"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q007.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-1.png"], "answer": "B", "explanation": "Use $(1-\\cos x)\\ln(1+x^2)\\sim \\tfrac12x^4$, $x\\sin x^n\\sim x^{n+1}$, and $e^{x^2}-1\\sim x^2$.", "methods": []}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q008", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 8, "question_type": "choice", "score": 3, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["拐点", "导数应用"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q008.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-1.png"], "answer": "C", "explanation": "Compute $y''=4(3x^2-12x+11)$. It has two distinct real zeros and changes sign at both.", "methods": []}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q009", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 9, "question_type": "choice", "score": 3, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["极值", "导数单调性"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q009.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-1.png"], "answer": "A", "explanation": "Let $F(x)=f(x)-x$. Then $F(1)=F'(1)=0$ and $F'(x)=f'(x)-1$. Since $f'$ is strictly decreasing, $F$ has a local maximum at $x=1$.", "methods": []}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q010", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 10, "question_type": "choice", "score": 3, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["导函数图像", "函数图像"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q010.md", "assets": ["images/q010_diagram.png", "images/q010_function.png", "images/q010_options.png"], "answer": "D", "explanation": "Read the sign changes of $f'(x)$ from the monotonicity of the given graph. Only option D matches.", "methods": []}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q011", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 11, "question_type": "solution", "score": 6, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["积分计算", "三角换元"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q011.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-2.png"], "answer": "$\\arctan\\left(\\dfrac{x}{\\sqrt{x^2+1}}\\right)+C$", "explanation": "Set $x=\\tan u$. Then the integral becomes $\\int \\frac{\\cos u}{1+\\sin^2u}du$. Let $z=\\sin u$.", "methods": []}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q012", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 12, "question_type": "solution", "score": 7, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["极限", "间断点"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q012.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-2.png"], "answer": "$f(x)=e^{x/\\sin x}$; $x=0$ is removable, and $x=k\\pi\\ (k\\ne0)$ are infinite discontinuities.", "explanation": "Take logarithms and use $\\ln(1+u)\\sim u$. The exponent limit is $x/\\sin x$.", "methods": []}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q013", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 13, "question_type": "solution", "score": 7, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["曲率", "弧长"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q013.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-2.png"], "answer": "$9$", "explanation": "Compute $y'$ and $y''$, then use the curvature-radius formula and the arc-length differential.", "methods": []}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q014", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 14, "question_type": "solution", "score": 7, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["反函数", "integral equation"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q014.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-2.png"], "answer": "$f(x)=e^x(x+1)-1$", "explanation": "Differentiate both sides and use $g(f(x))=x$ to get $f'(x)=(x+2)e^x$, then integrate and use $f(0)=0$.", "methods": []}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q015", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 15, "question_type": "solution", "score": 7, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["常微分方程", "积分计算"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q015.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-2.png"], "answer": "$\\dfrac{e^{\\pi}+1}{1+\\pi}$", "explanation": "Eliminate $g$ to obtain $f''+f=2e^x$. After solving for $f$, notice that the integrand is $\\left(\\frac{f(x)}{1+x}\\right)'$.", "methods": []}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q016", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 16, "question_type": "solution", "score": 9, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["微分方程", "最值"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q016.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-2.png"], "answer": "$(1)\\ y=\\dfrac14-x^2;\\qquad (2)\\ Y=-\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{3}X+\\dfrac13.$", "explanation": "The condition gives the differential equation $y-xy'=\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}$. Solve it and use the given point. Then optimize the enclosed area over the tangent point.", "methods": []}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q017", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 17, "question_type": "solution", "score": 7, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["相关变化率", "应用建模"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q017.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-3.png"], "answer": "$6$ hours", "explanation": "With $V=\\frac23\\pi r^3$ and $S=2\\pi r^2$, the law $dV/dt=-kS$ simplifies to $dr/dt=-k$, so $r$ decreases linearly. The given volume condition implies the radius is halved after $3$ hours.", "methods": []}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q018", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 18, "question_type": "solution", "score": 8, "module": "高等数学", "topics": ["积分中值定理"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q018.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-3.png"], "answer": "$(1)\\ f(x)=f(0)+f'(0)x+\\dfrac12f''(\\xi)x^2;\\quad (2)\\ see explanation.$", "explanation": "Use the first-order Maclaurin expansion with Lagrange remainder and integrate it on $[-a,a]$. Then apply the intermediate value theorem to the continuous function $f''$.", "methods": ["泰勒展开"]}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q019", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 19, "question_type": "solution", "score": 6, "module": "线性代数", "topics": ["矩阵方程", "可逆矩阵"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q019.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-3.png"], "answer": "$X=\\begin{pmatrix}1&2&5\\\\0&1&2\\\\0&0&1\\end{pmatrix}$", "explanation": "Rearrange the equation into $(A-B)X(A-B)=E$, so $X=(A-B)^{-2}$.", "methods": []}
{"question_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001_q020", "exam_id": "kaoyan_math2_2001", "exam_type": "math2", "year": 2001, "question_number": 20, "question_type": "solution", "score": 6, "module": "线性代数", "topics": ["基础解系", "线性无关"], "difficulty": "unknown", "review_status": "reviewed", "answer_status": "available", "explanation_status": "available", "source_file": "math2_2001_questions.md", "answer_source_file": "math2_2001_answers.md", "card_path": "questions/q020.md", "assets": ["images/source_pages/page-3.png"], "answer": "$t\\ne1,\\,-1$", "explanation": "The $\\beta_i$ remain solutions automatically. They form another basis exactly when they are linearly independent. The coefficient matrix relative to the $\\alpha_i$ basis has determinant $1-t^4$.", "methods": []}
